// EXPECT_STDOUT \🔥
//
// Registry 221.1 #832, the POSITIVE half -- and the two halves expect
// DIFFERENT things on purpose. D467 section 6: inside a backtick literal
// the escape set is exactly three (backtick, backslash, dollar), and any
// other character after a backslash passes through as TWO characters. That
// is what makes `` regex`\d{3}` `` work without doubling.
//
// So here the backslash and the multi-byte character must BOTH survive into
// the value. Before #832 the lexer skipped two bytes and cut the character
// in half -- the same crash, reached through the other form.
//
// This one carries a four-byte emoji after the backslash.
module standalone.m832_backtick_esc_emoji_pos

fn main() Io -> () {
    println(`\🔥`)
}
